REPL means Read–Eval–Print Loop.

It is an interactive Python environment where you can type Python code one line at a time and immediately see the result.
We can do this in terminal by typing python comand.

What each letter means
R — Read → Python reads what you type.
E — Eval → Python evaluates/runs it.
P — Print → Python shows the result.
L — Loop → It waits for your next command.